    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Limestone transforms into Marble and Sandstone transforms into Quartzite via thermal/contact metamorphism.",
        "The progressive regional metamorphic sequence of shale is: Slate -> Phyllite -> Schist -> Gneiss.",
        "Foliation develops predominantly under high directional pressure during regional metamorphism."
      ],
      "id": "1mpmwfd"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Contact (thermal) metamorphism occurs when host rocks are altered primarily by extreme heat from adjacent magma intrusions.",
        "Regional metamorphism affects vast geological areas driven by high pressure and temperature during mountain-building tectonic events.",
        "Dynamic metamorphism occurs along fault zones where intense mechanical stress fractures and deforms rocks without significant heat.",
        "Hydrothermal metamorphism takes place when hot, chemically active fluid percolates through rock fractures, altering mineral compositions."
      ],
      "id": "mdoyvc2"
    }
